{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDhPA7MD4zEqC1kQWstJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E10, E11 and E12 and saved the result in `agent/brace-findings.json`. `validate_findings.py --fix --batch E10,E11,E12 --before-challenges` reports `Valid` with two gaps and one needs_evidence. I did not run challenges.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| E10 (G1) | gap | The agent's database role can only SELECT and INSERT on `audit_events` (`migrations/001_init.sql:121`), and no tool can touch audit rows. But the payments call to the external vendor sends no run, trace or instance id (`app/tools/payments.py:33`). Its idempotency key is never stored in the audit record. The receipt is stored only after success (`app/loop.py:95`), and `tool_error` (`app/loop.py:87`) records no vendor id. A payment that times out after the vendor accepted it cannot be traced to an instance. |\n| E11 (G2) | gap | There is no hash chain, signature, sequence number or gap alert (`app/audit.py:67` only hashes tool results). The agent's own role can read every tenant's audit rows (`migrations/001_init.sql:121`), though no code reads them. Retention is not set anywhere in the repo, so E11.1 is `unknown`. E11.4 is `yes`: the proposal and authorization records are written before the tool runs (`app/loop.py:55,68,83`). |\n| E12 (G3) | needs_evidence | This item has no code checks. The repo has only fleet and tenant halts (`app/killswitch.py`) and one Slack budget alert (`app/loop.py:180`). I found no runbook, impact query, tool quarantine, responder routing or named reporting owner. |\n\n- **E10.1 is `unknown`:** the gateway, ERP and payments services are outside the repo. No trace or correlation header is sent to them.\n- **Prescan:** its 7 hits are for B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05. None belongs to E10–E12, so I resolved none.\n- **Injected instruction:** `tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt:21